# script/config/mainnet-token-decimals.env
# PB3.5b2 (PB-D27 (ii)) -- the STANDARD-slot decimals table: 45 unique mainnet token literals
# mapped to their real ERC-20 decimals. Derived on a mainnet fork with no broadcast by
# test-stubs/DeployTestnetStubs.s.sol and captured verbatim from its _emitDecimalsMap output.
# Mainnet truth, not environment-specific -- committed once, valid wherever the stub deploy runs.
# The Sepolia stub deploy reads these instead of calling decimals() on a mainnet literal that
# carries no code there; the read is fail-fast with no default, so a missing key reverts the run.
# Held here rather than appended to test-stubs/sepolia-stubs.env because that file is regenerated
# wholesale from the live broadcast at PB3.5i, which would make the consumer file rewrite its own
# producer. Do not hand-edit -- regenerate via the fork run.
# PB3.5 STANDARD-slot decimals table (mainnet-derived; stable across environments)
